build: 2026-06-30 v10.76.49 (Stable audio — no dropouts/crackle · Visuals tidy)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Two asks: stable audio (keine Aussetzer / kein Kratzen) + a tidier Visuals section
  (no half-built stubs, regulate what we already have).
  • AUDIO STABILITY (the dropouts/crackle): an audio-thread audit found the polyphonic
    synth could run up to 768 additive partials per sample (12 voices × 64 harmonics) — far
    over a phone's real-time budget on dense chords, so the render missed its deadline →
    buffer underruns heard as dropouts/crackle. Regulated WITHOUT a new subsystem, just
    sane caps: voices 12→8, harmonics 64→32 (still rich — most energy is in the first ~16),
    and the audio buffer 256→512 frames (render deadline 5.3 ms→10.7 ms, still well under
    the 15 ms limit). Net: worst-case partials drop ~3× AND there's 2× more time to render
    them — dense chords now stay inside the deadline. The deliberate 2-voice unison
    "richness" is untouched. (Next levers if anything still crackles: a one-time pop when
    switching to the named instrument patches — a small allocation that should move off the
    audio thread — and a denormal-flush in release tails; both noted for a focused follow-up.)
  • VISUALS TIDY: the fully-built "Prism" look (spectral dispersion) was implemented in the
    shader but never shown in the picker — now added to both the Look strip and the Blend
    strip, so every shipped look is reachable. Deleted a dead 271-line compute-shader stub
    (VisualRendererKernels.metal — five kernels, zero wiring) — exactly the kind of unfinished
    stub to keep out. No behaviour change beyond Prism becoming selectable.
  Build-checked. Test: 10.76.49 → play a full chord-heavy take (with bio on) and listen —
  it should be clean, no dropouts/crackle. Open the immersive visual → "Prism" now appears
  in the Look strip and as a Blend partner. Tell me if any crackle remains (and whether it's
  steady, on patch-change, or in the silent tail — that points to the next specific fix).
